         "Rational",
         -32,
         11
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Differentiate both sides with respect to t, using the product rule on the mixed term: \\( 2x\\frac{dx}{dt} - \\left(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\,y + x\\frac{dy}{dt}\\right) + 4y\\frac{dy}{dt} = 0 \\).",
         "rule_named": "implicit differentiation with respect to time"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Substitute x = 3, y = -2 and \\( \\frac{dx}{dt} = -4 \\): \\( -24 - 8 - 3\\frac{dy}{dt} - 8\\frac{dy}{dt} = 0 \\), that is, \\( -32 - 11\\frac{dy}{dt} = 0 \\).",
         "rule_named": "substitute after differentiating"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Solve for the requested rate: \\( \\frac{dy}{dt} = - \\frac{32}{11} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            -32,
            11
         ],
         "rule_named": "isolate the requested rate"
      }
